If you've been trying to get an H200, RTX 5090, or any high-end GPU on RunPod lately you already know how bad availability has gotten. You refresh the page, it says unavailable, you refresh again — and by the time it shows up someone else already grabbed it. In this video I show you the tool I built that solves this completely by automating the entire deployment process through the RunPod API.
The script monitors RunPod every second in the background and the moment your target GPU opens up it deploys instantly to your network volume with your template already applied. No refreshing, no babysitting, no missing pods while you're away from your computer.

✅ Works with RTX 4090, RTX 5090, L40S, RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, H200 SXM and more
✅ Attaches automatically to your existing RunPod network volume
✅ Pre-configured with the correct ComfyUI Manager template for your GPU's CUDA version
✅ Custom GPU and template support available

